<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<subsection xml:id="ch9-section-isobaric-coordinates-subsection-geostrophic" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Geostrophic wind</title>

    <p>
        As we learned in <xref ref="ch8-section-mid-latitude-synoptic-scale-analysis-subsection-geostrophic-balance" text="custom">Chapter 8</xref>,
        the geostrophic wind is given by
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-vector-reproduced" number="yes">
            \vec{v}_g = \frac{1}{\rho f} \, \hat{k} \times \nabla_z p
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        with components
    </p>
    
    <p>
        <md>
            <mrow xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-x-reproduced" number="yes"    >
                u_g
                \amp =
                -\frac{1}{\rho f}
                \left(
                    \frac{\partial p}{\partial y}
                \right)_z
            </mrow>
            <mrow xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-y-reproduced" number="yes"    >
                v_g
                \amp =
                \frac{1}{\rho f}
                \left(
                    \frac{\partial p}{\partial x}
                \right)_z
            </mrow>
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        where the subscript "z" has been added to
        <xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-y" text="type-global" /><ndash /><xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-vector" text="type-global" />
        to emphasize that <m>z</m> is used as the vertical coordinate when writing these equations.
    </p>

    <p>
        <xref ref="eqn-pga-isobaric-x" text="type-global" /><ndash /><xref ref="eqn-pga-isobaric-vector" text="type-global" />
        enable us to rewrite
        <xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-vector-reproduced" text="type-global" /><ndash /><xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-y-reproduced" text="type-global" />
        as
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-vector-isobaric" number="yes">
            \vec{v}_g = \frac{1}{f} \, \hat{k} \times \nabla_p \Phi
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-x-isobaric" number="yes">
            u_g
            =
            -\frac{1}{f}
            \left(
                \frac{\partial \Phi}{\partial y}
            \right)_p
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-y-isobaric" number="yes">
            v_g
            =
            \frac{1}{f}
            \left(
                \frac{\partial \Phi}{\partial x}
            \right)_p
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        Alternatively,
        <xref ref="eqn-pga-isobaric-x-geopotential-height" text="type-global" /><ndash /><xref ref="eqn-pga-isobaric-vector-geopotential-height" text="type-global" />
        enable us to rewrite
        <xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-vector-reproduced" text="type-global" /><ndash /><xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-y-reproduced" text="type-global" />
        as
    </p>
        
    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-vector-isobaric-geopotential-height" number="yes">
            \vec{v}_g = \frac{g_0}{f} \, \hat{k} \times \nabla_p Z
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-x-isobaric-geopotential-height" number="yes">
            u_g
            =
            -\frac{g_0}{f}
            \left(
                \frac{\partial Z}{\partial y}
            \right)_p
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        <md xml:id="eqn-geostrophic-wind-y-isobaric-geopotential-height" number="yes">
            v_g
            =
            \frac{g_0}{f}
            \left(
                \frac{\partial Z}{\partial x}
            \right)_p
        </md>
    </p>

    <p>
        Again, note that density no longer appears in
        <xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-vector-isobaric" text="type-global" /><ndash /><xref ref="eqn-geostrophic-wind-y-isobaric-geopotential-height" text="type-global" />.
        This is an advantage of using isobaric coordinates.
    </p>
</subsection>